silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors#tg_is_the_underlying_graph_of_freeg;_it_has_no_composition__ silm:hasLongDescription "The T(G) is the underlying graph of Free(G); it has no composition, so colimits don't exist there. G itself has no equation structure, so two paths to the same node need not be identifiable. Only after q : Free(G) -> C_G quotients by equiv_E does the colimit acquire universal force.  is T(G) is the underlying graph of Free(G); it has no composition, so colimits don't exist there. G itself has no equation structure, so two paths to the same node need not be identifiable. Only after q : Free(G) -> C_G quotients by equiv_E does the colimit acquire universal force." .
